## Antigravity Autonomous Workflow Constraints

### Commit Discipline:
- NEVER create generic, truncated, or repetitive commit messages.
- DO NOT commit intermediate or partial work. Only commit when a logical unit or test file passes completely.
- STRICT FORMAT: `<type>(<scope>): <precise imperative description under 50 chars>`
  - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `math`, `refactor`, `perf`, `chore`.
  - Scopes: `(limits)`, `(solver)`, `(payoffs)`, `(store)`, `(triggers)`, `(actor)`, `(deps)`.
  - Examples:
    - `fix(limits): enforce fail-closed check on NaN inputs`
    - `fix(solver): reject orders when margin budget is zero`
    - `test(bias): add strict temporal receipt assertion`
- BANNED PHRASES:
  - "apply security audit hardening..."
  - "add advanced mathematical..."
  - "complete institutional vrp..."
  - Any commit message matching a previously used commit message in the active session.
